#description Practice game 91, 2026-07-12. Reconstructed (Opus) from Jesse's scoresheet and final board photo; replaces earlier reconstructions.
#note Board-true reconstruction verified by an exact-score joint solve and a clean 100/100 tile-bag audit; it matches Jesse's scoresheet exactly (final Jesse 406, James 438, spread -32). Jesse moved first and OPENED WITH AN EXCHANGE of L and W (scoresheet "x2"). The endgame is the subtle part: after bingoing ESTERASE, Jesse drew the last 4 tiles in the bag (ADHV), played AH, then PLAYED THE V HIMSELF for 6 (V at H14, forming REV down column H - the scoresheet's lone "V +6"). James then went out playing only the two E's, forming VEE across row 14 for 13 (the third E on J14's triple-letter square; cross-word AME down column I). Jesse's leftover D (2 pts) gives James +4. Earlier reconstructions of this game erred here: one dropped the opening exchange and mis-ordered the players; another additionally handed Jesse's V to James (scoring the whole of VEE for one player) and wrongly dismissed the "+6" as a tally slip. Racks are played tiles only (partial) mid-game and true full racks in the endgame, as the importer requires.
